  "/v1/twins/{ref}/questions/{question_id}": {
   "post": {
    "description": "Ask a question of the catalogue (GET /v1/questions) to a twin. The body is the question's parameters.\n\n- `describe` (HN-02, D/M): Layers, sensors, period, mode and main settings, read from the configuration (no computation needed).\n- `water_flux` (HN-10, D/M): Mean, median, 5th and 95th percentiles of the flux q at the riverbed (z = 0) over the period, in m/s, positive downwards (infiltration: the river feeds the aquifer).\n- `exchanged_volume` (HN-12, D/M): Infiltrated, exfiltrated and net volumes over the period, integrated by trapezoids with the sign change cut at the zero crossing: m³/m², or m³ when an area is given.\n- `temperature` (HN-30, D/M): Simulated temperature in °C, linearly interpolated: one value (z and t), a profile T(z) (t alone) or a series T(t) (z alone).\n- `sensor_intervals` (HN-33, D/M): Per sensor: the measurement with its instrument interval (± z·σ), the simulation and, in mcmc mode with stored fields, the credible band (model) and the predictive band (a new measurement), with the share of measurements the predictive band covers. Arrays are sensor first: (3, T).\n- `provenance` (HN-43, D/M): Versions, data fingerprint, platform and duration of the computation, the command that reproduces it; the commits and state of each repository are in the provenance of the answer.\n- `residuals` (BN-31, D/M): Measured, simulated and residual (simulated − measured) temperatures per sensor, with the RMSE; option `intervals`: the credible and predictive bands.\n- `chain_data` (BN-34, M): Parameters, energies, acceptance and burn-in resets of the chosen chains, with the computed iteration of each kept sample; read thinning and iteration range as in the computation.\n- `sampling_layout` (BN-36, M): Chains, iterations per chain, burn-in, thin, total samples, fields per chain and the interval between them, space and time steps, store_fields and stored size; from the configuration, before or after the run.",
    "operationId": "ask_v1_twins__ref__questions__question_id__post",
    "parameters": [
     {
      "in": "path",
      "name": "ref",
      "required": true,
      "schema": {
       "title": "Ref",
       "type": "string"
      }
     },
     {
      "in": "path",
      "name": "question_id",
      "required": true,
      "schema": {
       "title": "Question Id",
       "type": "string"
      }
     }
    ],
    "requestBody": {
     "content": {
      "application/json": {
       "schema": {
        "anyOf": [
         {
          "additionalProperties": true,
          "type": "object"
         },
         {
          "type": "null"
         }
        ],
        "description": "Parameters of the question (see params_schema).",
        "title": "Params"
       }
      }
     }
    },
    "responses": {
     "200": {
      "content": {
       "application/json": {
        "schema": {
         "$ref": "#/components/schemas/AnswerOut"
        }
       },
       "application/x-npz": {}
      },
      "description": "Answer, as JSON or as an npz archive."
     },
     "404": {
      "content": {
       "application/json": {
        "schema": {
         "$ref": "#/components/schemas/ErrorOut"
        }
       }
      },
      "description": "Not Found"
     },
     "409": {
      "content": {
       "application/json": {
        "schema": {
         "$ref": "#/components/schemas/ErrorOut"
        }
       }
      },
      "description": "Conflict"
     },
     "422": {
      "content": {
       "application/json": {
        "schema": {
         "$ref": "#/components/schemas/ErrorOut"
        }
       }
      },
      "description": "Invalid request or parameters."
     }
    },
    "summary": "Ask"
   }
  },
